// expect: refused
// why: a variant is reachable bare, so it shares one namespace with structs, enums and functions
// from: issues/lang/0114

// `Thing(7)` here resolves to the *variant*, not the struct — and the checker used to say so only as
// a consequence: `wrong number of arguments to the constructor`, at the call, naming neither
// declaration. In the other order it said nothing at all and the program compiled. The reference
// refuses both with `duplicate name`, and the two lists this compiler keeps — one of file-scope
// names, one of variant names — were never compared with each other.
export enum E {
  Nothing,
  Thing(i32 x),
}

export struct Thing {
  i32 y;
}

export Thing make() { return Thing(7); }
